     The problem:[0m[2m between checking `[0m[2mjob[0m[2m["status"] ==[0m[2m "pending"`[0m[2m and setting it[0m[2m to `"[0m[2mprocessing"[0m[2m`, there's an[0m[2m `await asyncio.sleep[0m[2m(0.01[0m[2m)`. During[0m[2m that[0m[2m sleep, control[0m[2m yields[0m[2m to the event[0m[2m loop, and another[0m[2m coroutine ([0m[2manother worker) can[0m[2m also enter `[0m[2mdequeue()[0m[2m`, find the same[0m[2m job still marked as[0m[2m "[0m[2mpending",[0m[2m and pick[0m[2m it up too[0m[2m. This[0m[2m is a classic TO[0m[2mCTOU ([0m[2mtime-of-check-to[0m[2m-time-of-use[0m[2m) race condition.[0m[2m
     
     The fix: set[0m[2m the status to "[0m[2mprocessing" atom[0m[2mically before yielding control[0m[2m. The simplest[0m[2m fix[0m[2m is to move[0m[2m the status change[0m[2m before the `[0m[2mawait`:[0m[2m
     ```python
