     But[0m[2m wait, even[0m[2m this[0m[2m isn[0m[2m't fully safe in[0m[2m an[0m[2m async context because between[0m[2m the `[0m[2mif job[0m[2m["status"] ==[0m[2m "pending"` check[0m[2m and the assignment[0m[2m `job["status[0m[2m"] = "processing[0m[2m"`, there's[0m[2m no `[0m[2mawait`,[0m[2m so there[0m[2m's no yield[0m[2m point. In C[0m[2mPython with[0m[2m the GIL,[0m[2m this is[0m[2m actually atomic at[0m[2m the bytecode[0m[2m level —[0m[2m no[0m[2m other[0m[2m coroutine can inter[0m[2mleave between these two[0m[2m synchronous operations. So[0m[2m moving[0m[2m the status assignment[0m[2m before the sleep[0m[2m is[0m[2m sufficient.
     
